# Keep truecopy's own tree LF everywhere. Skill content is hashed byte-exact
# (CRLF != LF — see loadSkillDir), so a committed truecopy.lock's hashes stay
# stable across contributor OSes only if the bytes don't get rewritten by git's
# autocrlf. `text=auto` still auto-detects binary fixtures and leaves them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured CLI output, not hand-written text: scripts/readme/terminal.mjs
# generates this file from a real run of the CLI, so its punctuation is the
# CLI's own. The public-text and redline checks read this mark from the base
# commit and skip wording findings on the file.
.github/readme/terminal.svg redline-protected
